@RestController
@RequestMapping("/api/orders")
class OrderController {
    private final OrderService orders;

    @GetMapping("/{id}")
    @PreAuthorize("isAuthenticated()")
    OrderDto get(@PathVariable long id, Authentication authentication) {
        return orders.findForUser(id, authentication.getName());
    }
}

@Service
class OrderService {
    private final OrderRepository repository;

    OrderDto findForUser(long id, String username) {
        return repository.findByIdAndUsername(id, username)
            .map(OrderDto::from)
            .orElseThrow(ResourceNotFoundException::new);
    }
}
```
*Authentication alone does not prevent A01. The query scopes the record to the current principal, and the response uses a DTO rather than exposing the entity directly.*

```java
@RestController
@RequestMapping("/api/orders")
class OrderController {
    private final OrderService orders;

    @GetMapping("/{id}")
    @PreAuthorize("isAuthenticated()")
    OrderDto get(@PathVariable long id, Authentication auth) {
        return orders.findForUser(id, auth.getName());
    }

    @DeleteMapping("/{id}")
    @PreAuthorize("hasRole('ADMIN')")
    void delete(@PathVariable long id) {
        orders.delete(id);
    }
}

@Service
class OrderService {
    OrderDto findForUser(long id, String username) {
        return repository.findByIdAndUsername(id, username)
            .map(OrderDto::from)
            .orElseThrow(ResourceNotFoundException::new);
    }
}
```
*The user-controlled ID is not trusted by itself; the query includes the current principal. Administrative policy remains a separate explicit check.*

